erLine.discount\nfields. Earlier backend0.4.38 requests retain their previous facet refusals.\n\nThe additional domain uses existing exact decimal cells and PostgreSQL numeric\ncomparisons. Original text such as9999999999.9900 is retained; nonrepresentable\nvalues refuse without rounding. Scalar/item projections, equality, relationship\nkeys and an explicitly selected typed page path share the declared domain.\nNative accepted model/catalog/runtime correspondence remains required.\n\nThe new backend also uses an original stable Record or Field ID when its authored\nname is absent. An authored name takes precedence, punctuation requires ordinary\nSQL quoting, and ambiguous matches refuse. Earlier backend selections remain\nname-only. Original accepted module and binding bytes are retained.\n\nExisting protected String/I64 candidate profiles, native permissions and frozen\nbrowser cohorts are unchanged. The compiler release does not complete B-008 or\npromote native acceptance cases. All132 original requirements and existing case\nacceptances remain in force.\n"}